      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kake%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Kake serves as the headquarters of the federally recognized Tlingit tribe, the Organized Village of Kake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kake%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early explorers faced conflict with the Kake, including a 19th‑century incident where two white trappers were killed in retaliation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kake%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Some scholars claim Francis Drake was the first European to reach the area near present‑day Kake in 1579.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
